###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Mixing energies are per formula unit (meV/unit), which has no unit individual. The fine-tuned models reach validation RMSEs of 'about 0.2 meV' and '5.0 meV/A' and mixing-energy MAEs converging to 'approximately 2 meV/unit'; approximate values are not encoded.
# - MatterSim-5M is linked to the registry model MatterSim-v1; the other foundation models are distributed checkpoints without registry rows. Their mixing-energy errors on the three databases are only in Fig. 2.
# - Only Model 16 of the 16 fine-tuned models is encoded as a run; the others differ in training-set composition (Fig. 4b).
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/zhou2026fine.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

